{"availability":"available","full":"Uzairkhan11w/DOEpro","name":"DOEpro","description":"Analysis of designed agricultural experiments in R.","category":"Design","language":"R","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-12T09:38:21Z","updated":"2026-10-07T17:17:56Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://doepro.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:54.955Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:54.955Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:54.955Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T18:42:54.955Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A free, open R package and Shiny application for the analysis of designed agricultural experiments. It brings the standard analyses used in field and horticultural research — ANOVA for the common designs, mean comparisons, data transformations and clear reporting — together in one accessible interface, and serves as a free, self-contained option for the kind of analysis researchers carry out in tools such as OPSTAT.","Paste your data straight out of Excel, choose the design, press Run analysis. You get the ANOVA, publication-format tables of means with SE(m)±, SE(d), C.D. at your chosen significance level and C.V. at the foot, automatic advice on data transformation, post-hoc comparisons, plots, a plain-English interpretation, and a report you can download as HTML or PDF.","Suggestions and feedback are welcome — write to the maintainer (uzairkhan11w@gmail.com) or open an issue in the repository."],"features":["Dr. Immad A. Shah — Scientist (Statistics), Division of Agricultural Statistics, SKUAST-Kashmir. ORCID 0000-0003-2761-5112 · immad11w@skuastkashmir.ac.in","Mr. Uzair Javid Khan (maintainer) — UG Research Student, Statistics, AAAMDC Bemina, Cluster University Srinagar. ORCID 0009-0001-6368-0977 · uzairkhan11w@gmail.com","Dr. M. Iqbal Jeelani — Scientist (Statistics), Division of Agricultural Statistics, SKUAST-Kashmir. ORCID 0000-0002-2974-2871","Pooled (combined) analysis over environments — when the same experiment runs across several locations, years or seasons, DOEpro runs the combined ANOVA (environment, treatment, and their interaction), tests homogeneity…","Several response variables at once. Select as many response columns as you like; each"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Uzairkhan11w/DOEpro/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"eca67b9040336227ee03d810055adb34c97b62138de872bc254f998639df1723","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:55.051Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:55.051Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A free, open R package and Shiny application for the analysis of designed agricultural experiments. It brings the standard analyses used in field and horticultural research — ANOVA for the common designs, mean comparisons, data transformations and clear reporting — together in one accessible interface, and serves as a free, self-contained option for the kind of analysis researchers carry out in tools such as OPSTAT.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Uzairkhan11w/DOEpro/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"eca67b9040336227ee03d810055adb34c97b62138de872bc254f998639df1723","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Uzairkhan11w/DOEpro/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:55.056Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T17:17:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Uzairkhan11w/DOEpro/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T18:42:55.062Z","hash":"eca67b9040336227ee03d810055adb34c97b62138de872bc254f998639df1723","originalBytes":13192,"storedBytes":13192,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["error","pooled","response","plot","each","factors","means","environment","doi","factor","one","replication","two","when","analysis","app","base","c.d.","crd","data","doepro","factorial","lsd","pdf","rcbd","single","split","strip","treatment","against","carries","cell","duncan","effect","environments